course: dictionary
lesson: 6090
title: One word, three meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Meter is a word with more than one meaning, so you need its context to know which one is meant. Look at the words around it. «A square with sides of 5 m has an area of 5 × 5 = 25 square meters.» Here the sides and the area tell you that meters measure length.
explain: «For example, a man knocks and says he has come to read the gas meter.» The words read and gas tell you that meter means a tool. It is a machine that measures how much of something is used, and it shows the number.
explain: Poems use meter too, but in a different way. In a poem, meter is the beat or rhythm of the lines. When you read a poem aloud, you can often feel the beat, like a drum tapping steadily.
fact: A meter is a unit for measuring length. It has 100 centimeters and is about one big step of a grown-up.
fact: A meter is also a tool that measures and shows how much of something is used, like a gas meter, a water meter or a parking meter.
fact: In poems, meter is the beat or rhythm of the lines.
fact: «Square meter» and «cubic meter» are used for area and space, and «100-meter race» is a race of 100 meters.
fact: In science, lengths are often written in meters, shortened to m.
exercise: «For example, a man knocks and says he has come to read the gas meter.» What is a meter in this sentence? | *A tool that measures and shows how much gas is used | A race of 100 meters | The beat of a poem | A unit for measuring length
exercise: «A square with sides of 5 m has an area of 5 × 5 = 25 square meters.» What does m stand for here? | *meters | minutes | miles | millimeters
exercise: Mia reads a poem and taps her foot to the beat of each line. What does the word meter mean in poems? | A unit of 100 centimeters | The beat or rhythm of the lines | *The beat or rhythm of the lines, which you can feel by tapping | A tool for counting money
test: «A smart meter shows how much energy the house is using right now and what it costs.» What kind of meter is this? | A unit for measuring length | *A tool that measures and shows how much is used | The rhythm of a poem | A parking meter that counts time
test: Sam needs a rope 3 meters long for the den. Which word tells you meter is a unit of length? | Sam | den | *long | rope
exam: Read this: «Electricity reaches your home through a cable, passes the meter that counts it, and goes to the fuse box.» What is the meter in this sentence? | *A tool that counts how much electricity is used | A unit for measuring length | A square with an area of 25 | The beat of a poem
